    "title": "Police arrest 3 in string of downtown Austin robberies that injured Army service member - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Erin Slaughter ,\n8 hours ago Austin, Texas — Three suspects are now in custody after a string of armed robberies in downtown Austin last month that left an Army service member seriously hurt. Police say the robberies happened around 2:25 a.m. on September 13 in the 500 block of East Sixth Street. Officers say a teenager took a gold necklace from a woman walking in the area, then pointed a handgun at her when she tried to get it back. A friend of the teenager threatened to shoot her. Read full article\n1",
